open workspace
    Prefill the editor with a Smalltalk counter example.
    Create Counter, increment twice, add ten, and read its value: twelve.
open object inspector
    Request current object inspection.
    Display placement, mailbox depth, root path and unavailable-reference context.
    Display active calls and outbound waits with their targets and chain identifiers.
    Preserve variable and method lists; wrap long diagnostic text.
close inspector
    Dismiss when Escape is pressed or the backdrop is clicked.
header
    Display the Ctrl+Enter shortcut.
retention display
    Omit the explanatory retention note.
interactive inspector
    Select or type a method and enter typed arguments.
    Send through MCP call, display result or error, refresh object fields.
    Follow object references in fields and results to their inspectors.
    Show only Class and ID in Live Objects.
method buttons
    Sort selectors alphabetically before rendering.
    Unary button clicks invoke immediately; other methods prepare arguments.
    Ignore method clicks while a call is pending.

Use native method parameter names and optional inspectorMetadata JSON for typed inputs.
Read declared property getters through MCP. Set and Enter call setters, then refresh every property.
Display read-only properties and getter/setter errors; never mutate raw fields.
Show optional declared return type alongside method inputs. Render omitted JSON scalar fields as zero, empty string or false.

Header and inspector link to method browser and object graph. Responsive graph/detail overlay offers search, mode switches, fit, refresh and close.

Inspector adds assisted workspace controls and refreshes their receiver context after inspection.

Main output and explicit method/property calls preserve typed results. Add result shelf, recording controls and view area. Add retained-result arguments and character wire support.

Add debugger and message trace panels. Inspector Debug method opens the selected receiver. Skip automatic property/view calls during an active debug session; fields and debugger control remain available.

Source panel contains class editor, history, revision preview, working diff, saved-file commit message/action and Git object link, with responsive stacked panes.

Add Clone and Clone and edit to inspectors; display definition version/origin. Add the Wiring editor and an Open graph action for Wiring instances.

Inspector adds asynchronous send and a snapshot-based Promise panel; graph toolbar adds asynchronous run.

Toolbar comes from Workbench; fixed editor access remains available. Examples support isolated run/check, editing and object inspection.

Selector refactoring panel contains original/replacement names, class scope, preview and per-file save controls.

Add responsive Workbench visual editor and View designer panels, selection trees, property controls, live previews, JSON mode, save/reload/close actions and layout editing controls.

Offer Open control in designer when inspecting a live control.


The page composes the shared visual theme and layout behavior. Render a header, ordered tool sidebar, labelled expression/output area and searchable object list. The inspector separates Interface, Methods, State and Workspace into tab panels. Keep object actions in an expandable group and runtime details collapsed. Preserve section on refresh and give newly opened dialogs keyboard focus.


The Playground empty output offers discovery actions. Object inspectors expose property shortcuts, matching examples, selector suggestions, method navigation and debugger actions; results include Save as example.
The expression heading includes Load starter: object/messages, Explore files and Run a command templates, plus Restore my expression after a starter is selected. Choosing a template fills the editor; Run expression remains the execution action.
